{
  "$comment": "DronaHost blueprint data, read by check-content (schemas/blueprints.ts). Source: rules/page-blueprints.md and project/page-map.md. Counts, required sections and order for C1 come straight from the blueprint. For C2 to C15 the publish minimum is the number of required sections, and the word ranges for C10 to C15 that the blueprint does not state were confirmed by the owner on 2026-10-10 (decision 55). C1 was revised on 2026-10-09 (conversion review): WhyChoose, MigrationRequest, ProofBar and Evidence were added, and the answer and the timeline moved off Home. Revised 2026-10-09 (E-E-A-T review): every page blueprint ends with PageProvenance (who reviewed the page, when, how to report an error) before the closing CTABand, required on money, decision, trust and about pages; HonestLimits (what we do not do) joins C1, C2, C6 and C8. Revised 2026-10-10: the section maximum of C5, C9, C10c, C10d and C15 was raised by one so the appended PageProvenance fits. Revised 2026-10-10 (owner, decision 58): C1 is the brand home page of a global brand: a console hero with a one-field migration form, ratings, advantages, solutions, the ecosystem, reviews, the migration steps, the lead form, FAQ, provenance and the closing action. No prices on Home (prices appear only on /pricing). No PathRouter, PricingPlans, WhyChoose, HonestLimits or HelpAndPolicies on Home. Revised 2026-10-11 (owner, decision 60): ProductCards (four product cards with a button each, no prices) sits straight under the hero, and the section maximum rose from 12 to 13. Revised 2026-10-11: C2 names the feature grid BentoGrid, the section type the page system renders (there is no FeatureGrid section type); no content rule changed. Decision 62 (owner, 2026-10-11): C2 allows up to 1,800 words, and PathRouter (who it is for) and Meaning (managed or regular hosting) may follow the AnswerBlock. Decision 63 (2026-10-11): ProcessTimeline (the move) follows the AnswerBlock, because the WordPress hosting page targets wordpress hosting with free migration. Decision 68 (2026-10-11): ReviewsShowcase (the approved migration case study) may follow PricingPlans. Decision 76 (2026-10-12): RenewalCost (a three-year cost table computed from the pricing file) may follow BentoGrid or FeatureSpotlight. Decision 77 (2026-10-14): VideoEmbed (one real, captioned, click-to-load video) may follow the AnswerBlock on content pages (C2, C4 to C9, C12; C13 near the end); it is never required. Decision 78 (2026-10-24): PlanGuide (which plan fits which stage, rendered from the pricing file) may follow Meaning on C2 pages.",
